# src/features/

Each subdirectory is a CQRS module following the command/query separation pattern.

## Module structure

```
<moduleName>/
├── <moduleName>.routes.ts          ← Hapi plugin — creates the repo, handlers, buses, controller, registers routes
├── commands/                       ← write operations
│   ├── create-<moduleName>.command.ts
│   ├── create-<moduleName>.handler.ts
│   ├── update-<moduleName>.command.ts
│   ├── update-<moduleName>.handler.ts
│   └── delete-<moduleName>.handler.ts  (command + handler in one file)
├── queries/                        ← read operations
│   ├── get-<moduleName>.query.ts
│   ├── get-<moduleName>.handler.ts
│   ├── list-<moduleName>s.query.ts
│   └── list-<moduleName>s.handler.ts
├── domain/                         ← pure domain — no framework dependencies
│   ├── <moduleName>.entity.ts
│   ├── <moduleName>.repository.interface.ts
│   └── <moduleName>.events.ts
├── infrastructure/                 ← framework adapters
│   ├── bus.ts                      ← CommandBus + QueryBus (simple in-process dispatcher)
│   ├── <moduleName>.controller.ts  ← Hapi request/h handler methods
│   └── <moduleName>.repository.ts  ← one per ORM (in-memory, Prisma, TypeORM, Mongoose)
└── dto/                            ← data transfer objects
    ├── create-<moduleName>.dto.ts
    └── <moduleName>.response.ts
```

## Writing a new feature

1. Define the entity in `domain/<moduleName>.entity.ts`
2. Define the repository interface in `domain/<moduleName>.repository.interface.ts`
3. Create command/query classes and their handlers
4. Write the controller methods (they receive Hapi `request`, `h` and use the buses)
5. Wire everything in `routes.ts`:
   - Create repository instance
   - Create handlers (pass repository)
   - Create buses, register handlers by command/query class
   - Create controller (pass buses)
   - Export `ServerRoute[]` and a Hapi plugin object

## Routing conventions

- `POST   /<module>`           → `controller.create`
- `GET    /<module>`           → `controller.findAll`
- `GET    /<module>/{id}`      → `controller.findOne`
- `PATCH  /<module>/{id}`      → `controller.update`
- `DELETE /<module>/{id}`      → `controller.remove`
